    "limitation": "Separate completed window with same firmware under root control. The complete dual-vs-USB-only acquisition-rate difference is not attributed solely to this budget branch."
  },
  "causal_scope": "Call graph counts one descriptor checkpoint plus n-1 fragment checkpoints, so a successful n-fragment message consumes n work units. In the documented synthetic encoder VOLT1 frame, n=3 at firmware MTU247: at idleAge2 the descriptor consumes first grace unit and the first internal checkpoint consumes the second, then waits between fragments. Actual SCHED +14567 checkpoints vs BL50 +14513 fragment successes (slightly different observation windows) corroborates fine-grained accounting, but is not a CPU-time measurement.",
  "fix_scope": "Keep descriptor checkpoint, replace per-fragment accounting with at most four-fragment batches or one elapsed tick. Per-fragment connection checks, payload CRC, queue/slot ownership, error classification and global WorkBudget policy unchanged.",
  "counter_contract": "SCHED.bt retains checkpoints/yields/maxBurstUnits fields, but checkpoint unit changes to descriptor boundary or bounded fragment batch; counts across firmware versions are not comparable as raw fragment counts.",
  "limits": [
    "fe/cg/stale/ctrlRetry zero means no such reported event, not proof of unlimited radio bandwidth.",
    "Firmware BL50 and SCHED counters have distinct receipt/query windows; do not force equal deltas.",
    "vTaskDelay(1) count is not measured blocked duration or CPU utilization.",
    "Frames valid at transport CRC/identity can still contain ADC X codes.",
    "No post-change HIL result exists in this report."
  ],
